{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"MariaDB is operational on node1 with an inventory database and an items table.","status":"satisfied","summary":"MariaDB is active and enabled; direct metadata queries show inventory and inventory.items, and an application transaction succeeds. The service and schema remain healthy after a verified node restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-99f2a7cff89d4d48","cmd-d48f059a429a410a","cmd-ccebb1bb58e34ef2"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"A usable local MariaDB application account is configured for the inventory database.","status":"satisfied","summary":"inventory_app@localhost exists with SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, and DELETE privileges. Authentication through the stored credential reports CURRENT_USER() as inventory_app@localhost and successfully performs a transactional insert and read before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d00cc27d3ed041eb","cmd-d48f059a429a410a","cmd-ccebb1bb58e34ef2"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"The generated application credential is stored in /etc/inventory-db.env with root-only access.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The creation audit shows a random hexadecimal credential used for both the account and environment file, while authentication proves the stored secret matches the account. The file is root:root mode 0600 with no group, other, or additional ACL access, and an explicit nobody-user read test is denied.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d00cc27d3ed041eb","cmd-d48f059a429a410a","cmd-ccebb1bb58e34ef2","cmd-84c7bf442a4a4bc2"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.74,"summary":"All principal mutations had clear task or mandatory restart-protocol roles. The initial package attempt changed nothing; the subsequent full Arch upgrade was a supported prerequisite after stale repository packages caused 404s. Database initialization, service enablement, required object/file creation, rollback-based probes, and reboot were causally relevant. No unnecessary troubleshooting experiment is evident. The main retai